### Update News

This endpoint is used to update a specific news item.

#### Request Body
- title (string, required): The updated title of the news.
- content (string, required): The updated content of the news.

#### Response
The response for this request follows the JSON schema below:

```json
{
    "type": "object",
    "properties": {
        "status": {
            "type": "string"
        },
        "message": {
            "type": "string"
        },
        "data": {
            "type": "object",
            "properties": {
                "id": {
                    "type": "string"
                },
                "title": {
                    "type": "string"
                },
                "content": {
                    "type": "string"
                },
                "updatedAt": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "format": "date-time"
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
```

### POST /news

This endpoint allows the user to submit news data to the API.

#### Request Body
- `title` (text): A brief title for the news article.
- `content` (text): The content or body of the news article.
- `category` (text): The category to which the news article belongs.
- `thumbnail` (file): An optional thumbnail image for the news article.

#### Response
The response schema for this request is as follows:
```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "status": {
      "type": "string"
    },
    "message": {
      "type": "string"
    },
    "data": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "id": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "title": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "content": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "category": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "thumbnail_url": {
          "type": "string"
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

A successful POST request typically returns a `200 OK` or `201 Created` response code.

### Retrieve News by Author ID

This endpoint makes an HTTP GET request to retrieve news articles authored by a specific author.

#### Request

The request does not require a request body. The endpoint URL should include the author ID in the path parameter.

- Path parameter:
    - authorId (string, required): The unique ID of the author whose news articles are to be retrieved.

Example:

```
{{host}}/news/author/N4wjTWpWspcoEAGVjgmw02l14312

 ```

#### Response

The response will be a JSON object containing the news articles authored by the specified author. Below is a JSON schema representing the structure of the response:

``` json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "articles": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "title": { "type": "string" },
          "description": { "type": "string" },
          "publishedAt": { "type": "string", "format": "date-time" }
          // Add more properties as per the actual response
        }
      }
    }
  }
}

 ```

### News Search

This endpoint makes an HTTP GET request to search for news based on the provided query parameter.

#### Response

The response of this request is a JSON schema representing the structure of the news search results. The schema will outline the format of the data returned, including the keys and their respective value types.

Example response schema:

``` json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "news": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "title": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "description": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "source": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "url": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "publishedAt": {
            "type": "string",
            "format": "date-time"
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}

 ```

### Auth Login

This endpoint is used to authenticate a user by submitting their email and password.

#### Request Body

- Type: JSON
    - email (string): The email of the user.
    - password (string): The password of the user.

#### Response

The response of this request is a JSON object representing the authentication result. You can document the response as a JSON schema to define the structure of the response data.

#### Response JSON Schema

``` json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "token": {
      "type": "string"
    },
    "user": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "id": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "name": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "email": {
          "type": "string"
        }
      }
    }
  }
}

 ```

A successful POST request typically returns a `200 OK` or `201 Created` response code.

### Request

This is a POST request to the `{{host}}auth/logout` endpoint to log out a user. The request body should be in JSON format and includes the user's email and password for authentication.

### Request Body

- email (string, required): The email of the user.
- password (string, required): The password of the user.


### Response

The response of this request is a JSON object representing the result of the logout operation.

### Response Body (JSON Schema)

``` json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "message": {
      "type": "string"
    }
  }
}

 ```

A successful response will have a status code of `200 OK` or `201 Created`.

### GET /journalist

